w_luc_note: Land-use change (agriculture, deforestation, and so forth) has been a net source to the atmosphere for the whole record. However, over time the natural land sink has been growing due to CO₂ fertilisation, and so the total land contribution switched from a net source to a net sink around 1989 (based on the Global Carbon Budget, GCB) or in 1970 (based on our model — see “Is the model's land sink too high?” below). 
