==== C2. pulse lab (vvH, 2100, 500) ====
takeaway co2: Release 500 GtC in 2100 and 66% of it is still in the air a century later; 63% after 200 years. Unlike other greenhouse gases (methane, nitrous oxide), which are chemically or photochemically destroyed, emitted carbon is not destroyed; it just moves between sinks. The result of this is that a share of carbon emissions is effectively permanent on a human timescale. 
fair note:  FaIR was run for a 100 GtC pulse released in 2030-2100, every 10 years; set the pulse to one of those to compare.  
notes:  
   How this is computed:  
  the model runs twice — once with the pulse and once without, from 
  identical starting conditions — and the difference between the two 
  is the pulse's effect.
  
