==== I. Keeling / isotope takeaway ====
k i0 t: 1957.958333  neighbours: 1957.875000 1957.958333 1958.041667  abs: 0.125 0.041666666666742458 0.041666666666742458 
k_takeaway: The model produces 317 ppm in 1957, rising to 427 ppm today; the measured value is about 424 ppm. The model's inputs are emissions, global temperature, an ENSO index, volcanic aerosol light diffusion and nitrogen deposition, and its calibration data include the CO₂ level and seasonal cycle at both Mauna Loa and the South Pole. But it is not an abstract regression: it only adjusts quantities that stand for physical things. 
