i_takeaway i0 t: 1849.958333 
i_takeaway: δ¹³C has fallen 2.38‰ since 1850 as fossil carbon diluted the air — the fingerprint that the extra CO₂ is fossil. Δ¹⁴C tells a different story: weapons testing nearly doubled it by 1964, and the rate at which it declines provides information about the speed of carbon exchange between pools. 

